    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="e7f16f1a-2016-5c6a-abc5-b96ea48593e1" activityNameId="93f3e0c4-5787-5536-9ca2-37f22f3aa487" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Dung slab</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Dung slab
The module includes a dung slab made of concrete and a drainage to the slurry store. Size: 64 m2. Lifetime of the building is 40 years.;
UUID: 5c8a8bd3-7fb4-3566-9ca2-3ab4e633ab9c
The inventory takes into account the use of construction materials and building machines for construction, repair and replacement including waste disposal and the transportation of the materials to the building site. Not taken into account were direct emission of the construction, disposal of production waste and the use of resources during utilization phase. 
Location: The inventory applies for Swiss agricultural buildings only, because of the solid method of construction.
Technology: The data of the inventory are based on one example of a typical agricultural building.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: Existing dung store space in Switzerland in 1996: 2'878'934 m2.
Sampling: The inventory is calculated based on a solid database of agricultural buildings. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5c8a8bd3-7fb4-3566-9ca2-3ab4e633ab9c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
